From 22cc4972b2fa8b99fc9f46fd68e2f1f9b78075ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab-admin <homelab-admin@homelab>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:20:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] listener: record the observed Spotify account, never
 refuse on mismatch

_captureIdentityBaseline used to mark the session contaminated when the
Spotify account's email differed from the account email, which made the
listener refuse to record. That is exactly the case a decoupled SSO login
produces, so it is now information: the baseline records the observed email
and display name, reports them through a new on_identity_observed callback
(persisted by Database.setSpotifyIdentity) and returns True.

Tracking a CHANGE of account mid-session is kept: _validateCurrentUser
rebaselines on a different Spotify id, logs a warning and records the new
identity, but continues recording instead of forcing a reconnect. The worker
surfaces that as an annotation on a still-HEALTHY listener, not DEAD. Only a
genuine login failure remains a credential failure that is not retried.

The Web API backfill's own cross-account guard now compares the OAuth
identity against the tracked Spotify account rather than the login email.
